00:00:49.900 --> 00:01:17.920
All right? Now, those days are called in Hebrew Chag. Rosh Hashanah is not called a Chag. Kippur is not called a Chag. Hanukkah is not called a Chag. Purim is not called a Chag. And why? Because the word Chag in Hebrew comes from the Chag, Chet, Vav, Gimel, which means a circle.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:33.600
So only the pilgrimage is called a Hajj because you go to Jerusalem and you come back to your home. You make a circle. Yet the Arabs were terribly creative.

