00:51:48.540 --> 00:52:14.800
Alright. Now, Ruach HaKodesh. It doesn't mean the Holy Ghost of Spirit, but the Spirit of the Sanctuary.

00:52:14.800 --> 00:52:32.120
Kodesh in Hebrew is the Bet HaMikdash. Kodesh HaKolashim is the spirit that is in the Bet HaMikdash. Ruach HaKodesh is the spirit of the Bet HaMikdash coming to us.

00:52:32.120 --> 00:52:52.120
Why? Because God resides in the Beit Hamikdash. That is the residence of the world on planet earth.

00:52:52.120 --> 00:53:13.280
Whatever God does or doesn't do is via the Beit HaMikdash. Ruach HaKodesh is the Ruach which resides in the Kodesh. And some of us are very fortunate to have this Ruach coming to them from the Beit HaMikdash.

00:53:13.280 --> 00:53:35.560
So therefore the Beit HaMikdash is not just a temple, is not just a sanctuary for the Jews, that is the residence of Borei HaOlam, the Kiddushah that we could have in this planet is via the temple of the Beit HaMikdash.

00:53:35.560 --> 00:53:54.800
And last point I'll mention before I go into something else is the fact that the only way that we could actually experience the Shekinah, the presence of God, in our tradition, in the Jewish tradition, is through the Bet HaMikdash.

00:53:54.800 --> 00:54:11.060
When the going robbed away the Bet HaMikdash, it means that they wanted spiritual castration of the Jewish people. Until today, we see that fight. Even so-called friends of the Jews, they say yes, but not Bet HaMikdash.

00:54:11.060 --> 00:54:32.340
Because deep down they know that once that we are together, but not just in space, in geometrical space, but through the cohesiveness of the Shekinah, we are a different kind of nation.

