Now the Torah says, you want to be happy? Now you can do it. You're an individual.

01:10:34.580 --> 01:10:44.580
Leave the house. Leave the well. Go out with the family. Go into the sukkah. Don't worry. You'll be okay. You'll survive. You'll survive. You'll be okay.

01:10:44.580 --> 01:10:51.580
You notice people on the Sukkah, we're all singing Chizmonim, eating L'am Balim, drinking, having a great time,

01:10:51.580 --> 01:10:55.580
we don't have adjectives like this at any party, it doesn't exist.

01:10:55.580 --> 01:11:00.580
Because we're happy with who we are, we're happy with the Torah, with the Misbah.

01:11:00.580 --> 01:11:02.580
And this is a celebration of Sukkah.

01:11:02.580 --> 01:11:08.580
The Simcha that comes from within, the Simcha that comes from who we are.

01:11:08.580 --> 01:11:13.580
And, you know, I'm not together with the Qalumun, but the truth,

01:11:13.580 --> 01:11:27.960
I'm thinking, I was talking with Moritz, I was thinking, you know, there's difficult times, you know, fighting going on, and bombings, and things like that.

01:11:27.960 --> 01:11:30.960
You know, we have the Jewish people, we're all going to the Sukkahs.

01:11:30.960 --> 01:11:33.960
You know, anybody who goes to Tegnitz, that's Tegnitz.

01:11:33.960 --> 01:11:34.960
He's tired, he doesn't care.

01:11:34.960 --> 01:11:37.960
But we know, we know HaKadosh Baruch Hu is going to protect us.

01:11:37.960 --> 01:11:41.960
We know HaKadosh Baruch Hu promised that the children of Abraham are going to be

01:11:41.960 --> 01:11:27.960
in the

01:11:43.960 --> 01:11:46.960
And we follow the ways of Abraham.

01:11:46.960 --> 01:11:47.960
We follow his ways.

01:11:47.960 --> 01:11:49.960
Where are the children of Abraham going to protect us?

01:11:49.960 --> 01:11:50.960
I believe this.

01:11:50.960 --> 01:11:51.960
It's going to be Kibbutz Qadriyot.

01:11:51.960 --> 01:11:53.960
And if there's going to be Kibbutz Qadriyot, who's the Kibbutz?

01:11:53.960 --> 01:11:55.960
It has to be someone like Kibbutz Qadriyot.

01:11:55.960 --> 01:11:56.960
Who is it going to be?

01:11:56.960 --> 01:11:59.000
as we saw. This is a

01:11:59.000 --> 01:12:00.820
show, yes,

01:12:01.340 --> 01:12:03.460
dark place, but Sukkot, no, we're happy,

01:12:03.720 --> 01:12:05.260
we feel confident, this is

01:12:05.260 --> 01:12:07.000
the Sukkot, a symbol of God's protection,

01:12:07.440 --> 01:12:09.300
and this is the real Sukkot that we all

01:12:09.300 --> 01:12:10.700
aspire to. Very nice.

01:12:11.380 --> 01:12:12.440
I want to say something,

01:12:13.020 --> 01:12:14.880
it's almost

01:12:14.880 --> 01:12:17.140
one minute to quarter to ten,

01:12:17.880 --> 01:12:18.820
and as

01:12:18.820 --> 01:12:21.320
Amy was

01:12:21.320 --> 01:12:22.580
speaking,

01:12:22.580 --> 01:12:24.140
I remember a beautiful

01:12:24.140 --> 01:12:26.640
phrase, and

01:12:26.640 --> 01:12:34.320
And, Mizmor Lelavit, Adonai, Ro'in, Lo Ehsar.

01:12:36.060 --> 01:12:38.060
And, I'll come to it in a minute.

01:12:38.260 --> 01:12:41.960
God is our shepherd, and therefore I'm not going to be wanting.

01:12:43.060 --> 01:12:49.920
And then we say, Ro'in Iman, Moshe Rabbenu, Yisro'en.

01:12:51.000 --> 01:12:53.540
And we go, Litne Adonai.

01:12:54.360 --> 01:12:55.200
Litne Adonai.

01:12:56.640 --> 01:12:59.640
What do you mean with me, I'm the right?

01:12:59.640 --> 01:13:02.440
Means to you, I am?

01:13:02.440 --> 01:13:07.640
That I'm walking ahead of God.

01:13:07.640 --> 01:13:11.540
How can I be walking ahead of God?

01:13:11.540 --> 01:13:15.040
Hold the criticism for just for a second.

01:13:15.040 --> 01:13:18.940
Means that God is behind me.

01:13:18.940 --> 01:13:22.540
And I'm walking ahead of God.

01:13:22.540 --> 01:13:25.940
What is the meaning of this imagery?

01:13:25.940 --> 01:13:50.780
We were shepherds. Shepherds of, not cows, of sheep. No, no, that's very important. Because when the shepherd is always behind the flock, and from behind the flock he guides, from behind.

01:13:50.780 --> 01:14:13.520
Now the sheep does not see the Ro'eh. And the Ro'eh has two instruments. Sheep techa and Mish'an techa. The sheep is a stick. You could hit.

01:14:13.520 --> 01:14:23.020
The Mish'an, I don't know how you say it in English. I know you say it's a step, but I don't know what a step is the Mish'an.

01:14:23.020 --> 01:14:28.020
I know how to say it in Spanish, Cayo, is, I don't know how you say it in other languages.

01:14:28.020 --> 01:14:33.020
The Mish'an is a long step that ends like in a curve.

01:14:33.020 --> 01:14:37.520
They call it in Spanish,

01:14:37.620 --> 01:14:41.520
I don't know whether staff,

01:14:41.740 --> 01:14:43.840
that is the meaning of the word staff.

01:14:44.040 --> 01:14:44.960
I didn't look at the dictionary.

01:14:45.620 --> 01:14:48.100
But it has to be the staff of the shepherd,

01:14:48.420 --> 01:14:49.280
of the Hebrew shepherd.

01:14:49.900 --> 01:14:53.480
It has like a curve.

01:14:54.900 --> 01:14:55.940
Like a what?

01:14:55.940 --> 01:14:56.620
Like a cane.

01:14:56.920 --> 01:14:59.220
Well, in Spanish and Latin,

01:14:59.420 --> 01:15:02.120
cane is the staff that does not have this.

01:15:02.120 --> 01:15:22.020
You understand? I know I have to look in the dictionary. Alright? What are these? Shevet is that long stick and you hit. Shevet musa. Alright? And then you have the Mish'an.

01:15:22.020 --> 01:15:38.620
What's the function of those things? God is behind the flock. He does two things. With a shavit he heads. And by heading, then the sheep start walking faster.

01:15:38.620 --> 01:15:57.620
But sometimes the sheep's strength is going to go, is going to fall down. He holds it with a curve thing. Like a hook. Yes? It holds the sheep.

01:15:57.620 --> 01:16:12.020
Shevtecha u'mish'antecha, with your Sheveh, ta, edem Mish'an, hemmah yinah hamuri, v'lau

01:16:12.020 --> 01:16:23.540
they are my guidance. I don't see you, but I know that you see me.

01:16:23.540 --> 01:16:36.180
And therefore, you want to take me to the place of pasture and so on. This is the image of

01:16:36.180 --> 01:16:47.180
of Bithaon Bar-onai. God is our shepherd, we don't see Him. And I'm going to finish with a beautiful story.

01:16:47.180 --> 01:16:59.180
Abra-Manel. One of my off-bands, good old days. And Spain, we've all heard of the peace-hacker

01:16:59.180 --> 01:17:10.180
from Gidalei HaChem HaTorah, Minister of Finance to the King, and he writes the following story,

01:17:10.180 --> 01:17:17.180
that in his presence there was some Jews that they had to convert, one of them became Christian,

01:17:17.180 --> 01:17:26.180
and the other people, they ask him, you once were a Jew, and now you are a Christian.

01:17:26.180 --> 01:17:34.180
Tell me, what's the difference between when you were a Jew and now that you are a Christian?

01:17:34.180 --> 01:17:36.180
What's the difference?

01:17:36.180 --> 01:17:44.180
When I, he is a Christian because he is God all over.

01:17:44.180 --> 01:17:51.180
I don't know if you ever were in a Catholic country, the whole of the, the RV, because it's all over. Yes?

01:17:51.180 --> 01:18:04.180
I could see God, but God cannot see me. When I was a Jew, I could not see God, but God could see me.

01:18:04.180 --> 01:18:07.680
and your life and your soul is in the water.

01:18:07.680 --> 01:18:10.180
This is a development through G-d,

01:18:10.180 --> 01:18:13.680
He is the Lord, the Lord of the Lords, the Lord of the Lords.

01:18:13.680 --> 01:18:18.680
So, I want to thank you very much to Yitzchak

01:18:18.680 --> 01:18:21.180
and to Sherin,

01:18:21.180 --> 01:18:23.180
to the house that always makes a place,

01:18:23.180 --> 01:18:24.680
to the Lord's house,

01:18:24.680 --> 01:18:27.180
and really one day we will be together

01:18:27.180 --> 01:18:29.180
in Sukkot, in Yatam,

01:18:29.180 --> 01:18:36.180
and enjoying Kissel Ola of Benek Moshiach, you know, this problem is Kacher,

01:18:36.180 --> 01:18:42.180
not Kacher, Shechitah is going to be Lidiatan, it's a fish. So there will be no problems,

01:18:42.180 --> 01:18:46.180
we're all going to be able to eat together, and all the rabbis, even, we have absolutely

01:18:46.180 --> 01:18:48.180
nothing to complain.

01:18:48.180 --> 01:18:50.180
And the Holy Quran says,

01:18:50.180 --> 01:18:52.180
The Lord God said,

01:18:52.180 --> 01:18:54.180
God will search for his servant,

01:18:54.180 --> 01:18:56.180
and will bring him to the right place.

01:18:56.180 --> 01:18:58.180
Here we have the Holy Quran.

01:19:18.180 --> 01:19:20.180
Amen.

